This is the code to what will be the most complete personalized sunday dashboard to have alongside NFL redzone, keeping track of bets, big games, and player props for your fantasy teams, all in one place for easy viewing.

Need `conda install streamlit requests` in your conda environment (streamlit 1.50 or newer).

To launch the dashboard, type `streamlit run dashboard.py` into the command line. (`pip install -r requirements.txt` also works for the install.)

It works with Sleeper and ESPN leagues. The site, league and who you are in it are part of the page's link (`?site=sleeper&league=<league id>&user=<sleeper username>` or `?site=espn&league=<league id>&team=<team id>`), so each person has their own link to bookmark. Opening it without them shows a welcome screen to enter them, and the League button at the top right changes them. ESPN leagues have to be viewable to the public (League Manager Tools, Basic Settings). All times are shown in Eastern.

Bets are stored in a Google Sheet when `.streamlit/secrets.toml` has `bets_sheet_id` and a `[gcp_service_account]` section (the service account's JSON key), so each person keeps their own bets. The sheet needs a tab named `bets` with the header row `user, league, season, week, team, spread, placed_at`, shared with the service account as an Editor. Without the secrets, bets are saved in the local `bets/` folder instead. When hosting on Streamlit Community Cloud, paste the contents of `secrets.toml` into the app's Secrets setting. Never commit that file.
